  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "zstd: fix leak of tvbs",
  "description": "# Summary\n- Fix leak of `tvbuff_t` in `tvb_uncompress_zstd`\n\n# Background & Motivation\n\nThe leaks are currently reported by running `tvbtest` with valgrind:\n\n```\nvalgrind --leak-check=full ./build/run/tvbtest\n\n==17501==\n==17501== HEAP SUMMARY:\n==17501==     in use at exit: 674,484 bytes in 19 blocks\n==17501==   total heap usage: 2,628 allocs, 2,609 frees, 2,619,716 bytes allocated\n==17501==\n==17501== 655,680 (320 direct, 655,360 indirect) bytes in 5 blocks are definitely lost in loss record 12 of 12\n==17501==    at 0x4848899: malloc (in /usr/libexec/valgrind/vgpreload_memcheck-amd64-linux.so)\n==17501==    by 0xCF5D718: g_malloc (in /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libglib-2.0.so.0.7200.1)\n==17501==    by 0xCF74B64: g_slice_alloc (in /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libglib-2.0.so.0.7200.1)\n==17501==    by 0x8699496: tvb_new (tvbuff.c:69)\n==17501==    by 0x86A2035: tvb_new_real_data (tvbuff_real.c:65)\n==17501==    by 0x86A31E8: tvb_uncompress_zstd (tvbuff_zstd.c:64)\n==17501==    by 0x10D19D: zstd_tests (tvbtest.c:769)\n==17501==    by 0x10D3A3: main (tvbtest.c:811)\n==17501==\n==17501== LEAK SUMMARY:\n==17501==    definitely lost: 320 bytes in 5 blocks\n==17501==    indirectly lost: 655,360 bytes in 5 blocks\n==17501==      possibly lost: 0 bytes in 0 blocks\n==17501==    still reachable: 18,804 bytes in 9 blocks\n==17501==         suppressed: 0 bytes in 0 blocks\n==17501== Reachable blocks (those to which a pointer was found) are not shown.\n==17501== To see them, rerun with: --leak-check=full --show-leak-kinds=all\n==17501==\n==17501== For lists of detected and suppressed errors, rerun with: -s\n==17501== ERROR SUMMARY: 1 errors from 1 contexts (suppressed: 0 from 0)\n```\n\nThis was recently introduced in https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/9060.\n\nThe cause of the leak was misuse of a composite `tvbuff_t`:\n\n```c\ntvbuff_t *output_tvb = tvb_new_real_data((guint8 *)output.dst, (guint)output.pos, (gint)output.pos);\ntvb_set_free_cb(output_tvb, g_free);\ntvb_composite_append(composite_tvb, output_tvb);\n```\n\n`output_tvb` is always leaked. The first call to `tvb_composite_append` adds `composite_tvb` to the chain of `output_tvb`.\nThe `composite_tvb` is returned. But calling `tvb_free` on `composite_tvb` does not free `output_tvb`.\n\nThe proposed solution is to remove use of a composite `tvbuff_t`. It may not be possible for a composite tvb to free the data of the appended or prepended tvbs. [`tvb_new_composite` notes this requirement](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/f2218ae5f0ef259199f624abcd3f57d12894fa5a/epan/tvbuff_composite.c#L185-186):\n\n> * A composite TVB references the concatenation of one or more TVBs, each of\n> * them MUST be part be part of the same chain (the same memory \"scope\").",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-01-02T02:08:18.252Z",
